# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/003_switch_basic_fallthrough.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_switch_basic_fallthrough
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = Deliberate switch fallthrough: stacked labels, statement-carrying labels flowing on, fallthrough into and out of a non-final default, negative labels, and break out of a switch from a nested block
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every controlling value is a small literal, staged through the volatile int vin
in the runtime variant, and every case label is an ordinary integer constant
expression with no duplicates. The largest accumulated value anywhere is 1000
and the largest label magnitude is 99, so no signed overflow is possible on any
plain int. There is no shift, no division, no remainder and no pointer
arithmetic. Every object is written before it is read: r is initialised in each
helper that accumulates and assigned on every reachable path in each helper that
selects, the static const input tables have initialisers, vin is assigned before
each read, and out[] elements are written before being printed. The statement
after the break inside the nested block of break_from_nested_block is
unreachable at run time but is well formed and reads no uninitialised storage.
No object is modified twice between sequence points; each volatile write and
each volatile read stands in its own statement. There is no aliasing, no address
is taken, no uninitialised storage is read, and nothing depends on padding bytes
or on the relative addresses of unrelated objects. No evaluation order is relied
upon: the helper calls appearing together in one printf argument list are pure.
The fall-through comments are removed by the preprocessor and cannot affect
semantics; they exist solely so the reference compiler recognises each
fallthrough as deliberate under its default diagnostic set.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is printed. Plain char is never used as a value,
which matters because char signedness was measured to differ across the four
targets: signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. Every
printed value has type int, which is 32 bits on all four targets, so no value
depends on the measured pointer and long width difference (4 bytes on i686,
8 bytes on the other three). No address, no pointer value, no sizeof result and
no floating-point value is printed. The label sets here are small and contiguous
enough that no target's choice of switch lowering strategy can alter the
observable result. All 12 cells are therefore expected to produce byte-identical
stdout, and no target restriction is needed.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
const_stacked=10 10 10 20 20 30
runtime_stacked=10 10 10 20 20 30
const_accumulate=15 14 12 8 16 32
runtime_accumulate=15 14 12 8 16 32
const_through_default=7 4 8 6
runtime_through_default=7 4 8 6
const_signed_labels=100 200 300 400
runtime_signed_labels=100 200 300 400
const_break_from_nested_block=1 1000 7
runtime_break_from_nested_block=1 1000 7
END
